@@ -141,0 +142,14 @@
+
+### Bun dsh live verification
+
+The isolated `chat.brain-dsh-live` scenario uses an explicit private
+`OMA_DSH_LIVE_CONFIG` file to connect its fixture provider to a real OMA model
+proxy. Credentials stay outside evidence. It runs Bun Brain processes, checks
+public approval, sandbox bytes, history and worker epoch takeover after SIGKILL,
+then kills a process during Bash execution and verifies unknown tool results
+become native failure results without replay. The CCRv2 replacement-input check injects a reply
+through JetStream; public `user.tool_confirmation.updated_input` remains rejected.
+After that injection the private turn completes but the public approval stays
+pending. The test asserts this limitation before terminating that session; it does
+not certify public approval editing or a completed public approval lifecycle.
+The scenario does not change backend production handlers or the dsh kernel.
